  {
   "id": "kclvduAnBgAJ",
   "from": "Myriam",
   "author": "6154fc1ad20f15c1",
   "date": "2020-07-27T15:41:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Any work-around for inability to get \"casewise\" residuals in lavaan?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Update on my previous post: <div><br></div><div>I realized that obtaining standardized residuals was just a matter of basic stats : (Residuals - Mean of residuals)/SD of residuals. Here is my code for other beginners like me. (Now that I think about it, I could have used a standardize function.)</div><div><br></div><div>#inputing residuals back into data frame<br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">mydata$M1.resid\r\n&lt;- E[ , &quot;M1&quot;]<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">#standardizing residuals</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">mydata$M1.zres\r\n&lt;- as.numeric(<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">              (mydata$M1.resid-mean(mydata$M1.resid))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">                /sd(mydata$M1.resid))<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div><div><b>Remaining question:</b></div><div>I am still wondering if there is a way to obtain Cook&#39;s distance. </div><div><br></div><div>I will look back at my stat textbooks, but if someone has an easy way to obtain them, I would be super grateful.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div>Myriam</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "o9hBhxzTDAAJ",
   "from": "Patrick (Malone Quantitative)",
   "author": "12fdd832cacb825e",
   "date": "2020-07-27T16:04:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Any work-around for inability to get \"casewise\" residuals in lavaan?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Just a thought--for casewise residuals, wouldn&#39;t the SD of the original data make more sense for standardizing?<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Jul 27, 2020 at 11:41 AM Myriam &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">myriam...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Update on my previous post: <div><br></div><div>I realized that obtaining standardized residuals was just a matter of basic stats : (Residuals - Mean of residuals)/SD of residuals. Here is my code for other beginners like me. (Now that I think about it, I could have used a standardize function.)</div><div><br></div><div>#inputing residuals back into data frame<br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">mydata$M1.resid\r\n&lt;- E[ , &quot;M1&quot;]<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">#standardizing residuals</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">mydata$M1.zres\r\n&lt;- as.numeric(<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">              (mydata$M1.resid-mean(mydata$M1.resid))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">                /sd(mydata$M1.resid))<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div><div><b>Remaining question:</b></div><div>I am still wondering if there is a way to obtain Cook&#39;s distance. </div><div><br></div><div>I will look back at my stat textbooks, but if someone has an easy way to obtain them, I would be super grateful.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div>Myriam</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
